<title>ESTONIA: EBRD PAYS 3.0 MLN DEM FOR MAAPANK STAKE.</title>
<headline>EBRD PAYS 3.0 MLN DEM FOR MAAPANK STAKE.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Maapank, Estonia's seventh largest bank, said on Tuesday it will receive a three million German mark investment from the European Bank of Reconstruction and Development (EBRD) for the purchase of Maapank shares.</p>
<p>In a statement, Maapank said that the EBRD's investment decision was based on previous negotiations with the EBRD credit committee, as well as the bank's auditor's report.</p>
<p>Swedfund has also decided to buy two million marks worth of Maapank's ancillary liabilities, Maapank added.</p>
<p>Maapaank is an unlisted bank and it's 1996 profit was 200,000 kroons.</p>
<p>-- David Mardiste, Tallinn newsroom +372 630 8400</p>
</text>
